$ grep -n "expanded_locator" src/am/ec_distann/generation_read.rs
3552:    expanded_locator: default!(bool, "false"),
4612:    use_expanded_locator: bool,
4638:    let owner_heap_tids = if use_expanded_locator {
5996:        let candidate = super::options::benchmark_expanded_locator();

Result: production sends `vec_ids` and the owner resolves them to the current row
TID itself (Task 221's `benchmark_expanded_locator` is the benchmark-only variant
that ships the TID from the coordinator). Because P1-1's sidecar holds one entry per
row-tier version keyed by that version's TID, whichever TID the owner resolves has a
same-transaction sidecar entry, so §3's "visible row-tier tuple with no matching
visible sidecar tuple = corruption" remains provable on the remote path. No blocker
here; recorded because it bounds what P1-1's version-exactness actually buys
remotely.

