$ sed -n 1821p crates/ecaz-cli/src/commands/dev/distann_multicluster.rs
         CREATE TABLE dm (id bigint, source real[], embedding ecvector);\n\

$ sed -n 1904p crates/ecaz-cli/src/commands/dev/distann_multicluster.rs
             (SELECT id FROM dm ORDER BY embedding <#> q.v LIMIT {top_k}) r;\n\

Result: attnum 1 is `id bigint` — fixed width, `pg_catalog`, not dropped, not
generated, not the indexed vector attribute (attnum 3). attnum 2 (`source real[]`)
is an array and is correctly excluded by seq-03 §1's allowlist. The recall/latency
query projects `id` alone, so the Task 222 mask is `Exact([1])` and the cover `'1'`
is an exact subset. seq-03 §6's candidate declaration is feasible as written.

Width bound check: the widest allowed type in seq-03 §1's ten-type allowlist is
`uuid` at 16 bytes (`bool` 1, `int2` 2, `int4`/`float4`/`date` 4, `int8`/`float8`/
`time`/`timestamp`/`timestamptz` 8). 16 attributes x 16 bytes = 256 value bytes;
16 null bits = 2 bytes; 258 total. The arithmetic in §1 is correct and far below the
~2 kB TOAST threshold, so `STORAGE PLAIN` cannot fail on a bounded entry.

